course: dictionary
lesson: 12786
title: Words that look easy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Effortless means done without trying hard, so it looks easy. When you meet it, ask: did the person seem to work hard, or did it look natural? «The skater spun across the ice with effortless grace.» The skater makes it look easy, so effortless means done without strain.
explain: Effort is the work or energy you put into something. Effortless is effort with the -less ending, meaning without. Look for clues in the sentence: «She had practised every day, so her piano playing sounded effortless.» The practice is the hard work, and the result looks easy.
explain: Use the check from earlier lessons. Swap in your meaning: «The skater spun across the ice without trying hard.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Phrases like «effortless ease» and «made it look effortless» show you how the word is used.
fact: Effortless is an adjective, so it describes a noun: an effortless jump, an effortless performance.
fact: «Effortless» means done without trying hard, or looking easy.
fact: «Effortless» can also mean natural and smooth, without strain.
fact: In sport and music, an effortless performance often comes from lots of practice.
fact: Phrases to remember: «effortless ease» and «made it look effortless».
exercise: «The dancer leapt across the stage with effortless grace.» What does effortless mean here? | Done very slowly and carefully | *Done without trying hard, looking easy | Done in the dark | Done while wearing heavy boots
exercise: «He made the high jump look effortless.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the jump looked easy. | high | *effortless | jump | he
exercise: Ravi has practised the violin for years. When he plays, the music sounds effortless. Why? | *Years of practice make the playing look and sound easy | He is playing without any practice at all | He is trying very hard to look tired | The music is loud and fast
test: «She gave an effortless smile as she answered every question.» What does effortless suggest about her? | Her smile was forced and tense | She had lost her voice | She was angry and upset | *She seemed relaxed and natural, without strain
test: Which word means nearly the same as effortless? | *Easy | Difficult | Slow | Heavy
exam: Which sentence uses effortless correctly? | She effortlessly stopped the bus from crying | The effortless rain fell hard all day | The boy lifted the heavy box with great effort, and it was effortless | *The gymnast landed the flip with effortless control
